---
import { evidenceUrl, url } from "../lib/specs";
const milestones = [
  { status: "Verified on hardware", title: "The ESP SDR demo works", text: "The user-operated live viewer delivered 2,706 verified frames over 60 seconds. Two earlier minutes also passed. Each restored and verified the original 4 MiB firmware. The localhost viewer closes before restoration.", proof: "docs/evidence/esp-demo-play-001/README.md", label: "Interactive demo and restoration", kind: "verified" },
  { status: "Fresh reception reproduced", title: "An owned BLE packet decoded", text: "Matched ten-bit/manual48 controls reproduced a complete owned BLE packet. The later control ladder retained null results and one short-read failure; full original restorations pass. Independent replay of 1,256 saved waveforms preserves both known packets after exact upper-eight-bit reduction. That supports the decoder and digital conversion, while live detection reliability and missed-event rates remain unproved.", proof: "docs/evidence/ble-bluez-control-004/README.md", label: "Current ladder control and measured plot", kind: "verified" },
  { status: "Cancellation reviewed · source timing blocked", title: "Source verification still exceeds its clock", text: "Historical preparation passes saved review: 49 jobs and both whole archives in 105.670 seconds under 165. Verifier and concurrent content spans of 75.134 and 30.320 seconds exceed the unchanged 13-second source allowance. No producer launched. Cancellation now passes offline review with 143 author and 24 independent host groups; current root transfer, full runtime proof and timing fit still precede source qualification.", proof: "docs/evidence/ble-primary-timed-source004-readonly-review/README.md", label: "Read-only proof and unresolved source gates", kind: "partial" },
  { status: "Verified on hardware", title: "RTL-SDR delivers useful reception", text: "The attached dipole received FM/RDS identifying WXJC. The receiver comparison is accepted; calibrated shared-signal sensitivity remains deferred.", proof: "docs/evidence/rtl-dipole-rds/README.md", label: "Current-dipole RDS proof", kind: "verified" },
  { status: "Clock correction reviewed · fresh runtime pending", title: "Forgix host preparation advances", text: "Configuration006 and register/synthetic runtime snapshots pass review. Two owned file/lock probes found clock finalization faults. The correction now passes independent whole software review, including 94 clock tests and actual subprocess failure controls. Fresh runtime verification and candidate rebinding remain pending. No FPGA programming, register readback or physical clock test ran.", proof: "docs/evidence/forgix-clock-finalization-followup/README.md", label: "Clock runtime, retained failures and next gates", kind: "partial" },
  { status: "64 KiB/s passes · 256 KiB/s loses data", title: "Forgix USB loss is measured", text: "The 64 KiB/s condition passes without loss. At requested 256 KiB/s, 15,530,520 payload bytes arrived over 60 seconds and 431 records were discarded, all accounted for. Full original-flash and factory verification passed. Maximum capacity and FPGA transport remain open.", proof: "docs/evidence/forgix-usb-ram-recovery/README.md", label: "USB measurements and retained failures", kind: "partial" },
];
---
<section class="project-checkpoint" aria-labelledby="checkpoint-title" data-project-checkpoint>
  <header><p class="eyebrow">CURRENT CHECKPOINT · OCTOBER 5, 2026</p><h2 id="checkpoint-title">The demo works. The next experiments have clear gates.</h2><p>Hardware results, software preparation and failed experiments are shown separately. The full RF and FPGA evaluations remain open.</p></header>
  <div class="milestones">{milestones.map(item => <article class={`milestone ${item.kind}`}><span class="milestone-status">{item.status}</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p><a href={evidenceUrl(item.proof)}>{item.label} →</a></article>)}</div>
  <div class="next-work"><div><p class="eyebrow">NEXT, IN ORDER</p><ol><li><strong>Complete the FPGA clock test.</strong> Clock finalization now passes independent software review. Refresh its runtime and candidate binding, then verify matching attachment, full preservation and current admission before one bounded diagnostic. Separate register and finite-stream qualification follow; host simulations do not supply physical proof.</li><li><strong>Fit verification into source timing.</strong> The <a href={evidenceUrl("docs/evidence/ble-primary-timed-source-001-failed/README.md")}>first timed attempt failed before source setup and was recovered</a>. The cancellation correction passes offline host review; historical verification still exceeds source frontwork. The committed instrumentation plan measures the full preparation cost before selecting an optimization. Complete current root transfer and full fresh runtime proof, preserving all original timing limits. Then prove current admission and actual source qualification before one separately frozen 180-second receiver condition. Capture-window coverage supplies no air denominator, reception rate, three reciprocal responses or original Trial B acceptance.</li><li><strong>Measure the FPGA transport.</strong> The 256 KiB/s MCU USB loss is not a USB ceiling. Qualify the separate finite FPGA FIFO and autonomous RP/host path, then measure sequence/CRC, backlog and loss at several rates before RF integration.</li></ol></div><aside><h3>What we need from you</h3><p>The 2026-10-05 06:39:08 UTC read-only USB survey finds the ESP and RTL-SDR, but no matching Forgix; it opens no device. Its preserved identity and factory return remain historical evidence. The historical documentary case remains intended-design evidence; current loading review needs fresh runtime and candidate binding for the reviewed clock correction. No further photo is needed for that software work. Reconnect the preserved Forgix for fresh operator gates. Actual clock and electrical timing remain unmeasured. The ordered S31 is still deferred.</p><h3>Will Forgix need wires to the ESP?</h3><p>A direct SPI path needs verified I/O and a common ground; Forgix retains USB to the PC. Internal clock/register/transport tests need no ESP wiring. PC-mediated processing keeps ESP capture gaps.</p><a href={url("fpga/")}>Transport stages and pin ownership →</a></aside></div>
</section>
<style is:global>
  .project-checkpoint { margin:2.5rem 0; padding:1.6rem; border:1px solid var(--rule); border-radius:12px; background:var(--surface); color:var(--ink); }
  .project-checkpoint header { max-width:64rem; margin-bottom:1.4rem; }
  .project-checkpoint h2 { font-size:clamp(1.5rem,2.7vw,2.2rem); line-height:1.15; margin:.5rem 0 .8rem; }
  .project-checkpoint header p, .project-checkpoint article p, .project-checkpoint aside p, .project-checkpoint li { color:var(--ink-2); line-height:1.55; }
  .project-checkpoint .milestones { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:1rem; }
  .project-checkpoint .milestone { padding:1.1rem; border:1px solid var(--rule); border-top:3px solid var(--accent); border-radius:7px; }
  .project-checkpoint .partial { border-top-color:var(--unverified); }
  .project-checkpoint .prepared { border-top-color:var(--muted); }
  .project-checkpoint .milestone-status { font: .65rem var(--mono); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.05em; color:var(--muted); }
  .project-checkpoint h3 { font-size:1.08rem; line-height:1.25; margin:.65rem 0; }
  .project-checkpoint article p { font-size:.9rem; margin:.7rem 0 1rem; }
  .project-checkpoint a { color:var(--accent); font-size:.88rem; }
  .project-checkpoint .next-work { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.45fr 1fr; gap:2rem; margin-top:1.5rem; padding-top:1.4rem; border-top:1px solid var(--rule); }
  .project-checkpoint ol { padding-left:1.2rem; margin:.7rem 0 0; }
  .project-checkpoint li { margin:.65rem 0; font-size:.92rem; }
  .project-checkpoint aside { padding:1rem 1.2rem; background:var(--surface-2); border-radius:7px; }
  .project-checkpoint aside h3:first-child { margin-top:0; }
  .project-checkpoint aside p { font-size:.9rem; }
  @media(max-width:1050px) { .project-checkpoint .milestones { grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); } }
  @media(max-width:650px) { .project-checkpoint { padding:1rem; } .project-checkpoint .milestones,.project-checkpoint .next-work { grid-template-columns:1fr; } .project-checkpoint .next-work { gap:1rem; } }
</style>
